  "body": "## Characteristic-2 shadows of rank-3 decoders: the anti-Fano bound by first-order jets, with a Lean-checked core (no \u03ba claim)\n\nPackage `research/char2-jets`. Model, cost formula and lemmas are those of the merged #1590 (exact decoders, Lemma A, Lemma B), of #2111 (three-total decoders, the sharp example `tied_min`) and of #2125 (where characteristic 2 starts to pay); the Lean project formalises the rank argument behind Lemma B and its characteristic-2 twin. This PR studies the incidence pattern of a configuration over a field of characteristic 2.\n\n**PROVEN (proofs in the README).** Lemma CR2 (a characteristic-2 realisation of the incidence pattern gives cost \u2265 v for every B) with its tropical / 2-adic corollary, and Lemma A (T \u2264 2) as a one-line corollary; Theorem B2 (the map \u03c6 with \u03c6(\u22121) = 1: cost \u2265 v \u2212 |H| \u2212 |F| + MAS(W[F]); no wild incidence and no harmonic line gives (A)); Lemma VCR2 (a valued realisation whose diagonal dominates every directed cycle gives cost \u2265 v) and Corollary J (a B-independent linear-algebra jet test); **Theorem T\u2032: `tied_min` (the anti-Fano configuration of #2111) has cost \u2265 12 for every admissible B, by a first-order jet around its Fano collapse, with no SAT call and no enumeration**; Lemma F (the first-order obstruction is a binary flow of even incidence count). The generic-rank / split bound is proved; its completeness (equivalence with (A)) rests on a standard matching min-max that is quoted, not proved, and checked on instances.\n\n**Lean (checked).** `lean/DecoderDuality.lean` formalises the core lemma `hadamard_diag_rank_sum`, Lemma B and Lemma CR2; no `sorry`, axioms `propext`, `Classical.choice`, `Quot.sound` only. It does not formalise B2, VCR2, Corollary J, T\u2032 or Lemma F. `verify.sh` does not need Lean (`LEAN=1` runs the build if `lake` is present).\n\n**CHECKED (exact, `verify.sh`).** T\u2032: the explicit jet satisfies (J1) on all 72 incidences and (J2) on all 12 lines, and 518 stored matrices B (217 optima, the full B, 300 random) have rank 12; stored CR2 realisations of 21 configurations are verified (all realise over GF(2) except `cex_min_1` over GF(4), so cost(`cex_min_1`) \u2265 19 for every B); `tied_min` is not CR2 over GF(2), GF(4), GF(8), GF(16); the 44 minimal non-CR2 sub-configurations (32 of six lines, tight); Corollary J on all 4095 sub-configurations of `tied_min` and on 1500 random all-harmonic configurations; Lemma A and B2 spot checks. **Recorded, not re-run:** the SAT enumeration of the 217 optima, 1889 of 1892 random configurations passing the jet test, the 400 B2 configurations, 300 wild-cycle configurations (all CR2), the split min-max on 300 instances.\n\n**Jet failures (CHECKED).** On three random configurations jf0, jf1, jf2 a harmonic line cannot be moved at first order, and the order-2 diagonal vanishes identically on the first-order tangent space, so jets of order 1 and 2 give no B-independent certificate there. (A) still holds on them: exact minimum cost 12 (jf1, v = 9) and 14 (jf2, v = 9); cost \u2265 16 for jf0 (v = 11; \"cost \u2264 15\" is UNSAT; the exact value is unknown).\n\n**Not claimed / OPEN.** No \u03ba gain, no word, no window closed. (A) at T = 3 is neither proved nor refuted. Open: the \"2-adic shadow\" conjecture (every configuration over Q has a characteristic-2 valued realisation whose diagonal dominates every directed cycle); whether the Lemma F flow obstructs at every order on jf0..2 (orders \u2265 3 untested); a theorem for wild cycles (three-term incidences), which \u03c6 breaks; the min-max behind the split bound.\n\n**Verify.** `bash research/char2-jets/verify.sh /fresh/dir` (python3 with python-sat and numpy, and `cc`; about one minute; step 0 checks `MANIFEST.sha256` and stops hard on mismatch). Optional: `LEAN=1 bash research/char2-jets/verify.sh /fresh/dir`, or `cd research/char2-jets/lean && lake build` (Mathlib at the pinned revision).\n\nPrepared by DreamingOfClouds with Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), via Claude Code; Apache-2.0.\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
